# Algorithms tdns-signer links an implementation for.
#
# Currently the same selection as cmdv2/auth/algs.list, but that is a starting
# point, NOT an invariant -- and locking the two together would defeat the
# point of running a signer at all. tdns-auth can sign its own zones; a
# separate signer earns its keep when the two ends differ, typically because
# the authoritative server sits on modest hardware and the signer does not.
# The signer is then free to use algorithms the primary could not carry -- the
# post-quantum ones especially, which are markedly more expensive to sign with.
#
# The requirement is coverage, not equality: this list must contain every
# algorithm a DNSSEC policy applied here names. A policy naming an algorithm
# this binary did not link quarantines that zone at load with the algorithm
# named, so the failure is localised and legible rather than silent.
#
# One registry NAME per line (see dnssec-algorithms/registry/registry.go).
# genalgs resolves each name to its codepoint, caps, package, and lib group,
# checks the lib is installed, and emits registered_algs.go + metadata_algs.go.
# Pure-Go (no lib needed):
MLDSA44
MLDSA65
MLDSA87
SLHDSA128S
# liboqs-backed:
FALCON512
FALCON1024
MAYO1
MAYO2
MAYO3
MAYO5
SNOVA24_5_4
SNOVA37_17_2
SNOVA25_8_3
CROSSRSDPG128SMALL
# SQIsign reference lib:
SQISIGN1
# QR-UOV reference lib:
QRUOV_Q31_L3
